    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense enters today\u2019s slate with a clear focal point in **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 78.38 efficiency score makes him the undisputed engine of the lineup against Dean Kremer. Despite the lack of an elite pitching matchup, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a strong platoon advantage and a premium spot at the top of the order, making him our highest-projected asset for Roto production. Similarly, **Jacob Wilson** (64.36) and **Kyle Tucker** (64.04) are high-leverage starts; **Jacob Wilson** leverages a 10% park factor boost against Freddy Peralta, while **Kyle Tucker** remains a plug-and-play staple despite a neutral platoon matchup, as his underlying base projection anchors the outfield.\n\nOur most difficult decision of the day involved **Wade Meckler** (38.79), who finished just outside the starting threshold. While **Wade Meckler** offered potential utility as an order-one spark plug, the optimizer ultimately pivoted to the superior raw output and platoon-neutral efficiency provided by **Dominic Smith** and **Coby Mayo**. We are monitoring the rain risk at the stadium affecting **Drake Baldwin**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Dominic Smith**; a 31% chance of precipitation poses a slight volatility risk for these three, particularly for **Drake Baldwin** at the catcher position. \n\nOn the injury front, the absence of **Jordan Westburg**\u2014along with the scheduled off-days for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Heliot Ramos**\u2014has condensed our depth. We are closely watching the confirmed lineups for **Drake Baldwin**, **Liam Hicks**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Coby Mayo**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Andy Pages**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Dominic Smith** to ensure our batting order assumptions hold true. Should any of these bats move down the order, we are prepared to pivot to the remaining bench depth, including **Nasim Nunez**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Josh Jung**, **Curtis Mead**, or **Luis